<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20403" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">helxīnē</span></b> ,
		ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑλξίνη</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A prickly plant</i>, otherwise unknown, <i><span class="en">Plin. 21,
				16, 56, § 94</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A plant</i>, <i>otherwise called</i>
			perdicium: Parietaria officinalis, Linn.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 22,
				17, 19, § 41</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
